  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "Ledger-minded dwarves who weigh kinship, memory, and profit on the same carefully balanced scale.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Ormaz-Kheled carve markets into their lower halls and keep ancestor vaults behind counting rooms, believing the dead should witness the bargains of the living. Their guild-clans argue fiercely, but records, witness marks, and inherited custom usually keep the peace. They are more open than most dwarves, especially to traders who respect contracts and the dignity of old names."
